From 3815c63dc8c1c590ad203ad2b835058ddaa54273 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EberhartLeberhart <eberhartleberhart585@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:36:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: redmi_a5: enable DMA-BUF heaps

The VSP video decoder takes its buffers as dma-bufs. Enable the DMA-BUF heap framework and the system heap, so user space can allocate buffers from /dev/dma_heap/system. Verified on a Redmi A5: a 1 MiB system-heap buffer is mapped through the VSP IOMMU at IOVA 0x2ff00000.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W8YQkFAqgbw689knydrHtG
---
 arch/arm64/configs/redmi_a5_defconfig | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/redmi_a5_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/redmi_a5_defconfig
index 120681c28..456c9c0ff 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/redmi_a5_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/redmi_a5_defconfig
@@ -1057,3 +1057,5 @@ CONFIG_ZSMALLOC=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_ZSTD=y
 CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_ZSTD=y
+CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS=y
+CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM=y
-- 
2.43.0

